{"code":"def group_holdout_indices(groups, holdout_group):
    train_indices = []
    validation_indices = []

    for index, group in enumerate(groups):
        if group == holdout_group:
            validation_indices.append(index)
        else:
            train_indices.append(index)

    return {
        'train': train_indices,
        'validation': validation_indices
    }","status":"pending_evaluation","topic_id":"mlf_021","exercise_id":"mlf_021_group_holdout_indices_v1","interpretation":"This function creates a group-based validation split by keeping all records from one selected group, such as a production line, entirely outside training. For example, if Line_B is held out, the model is trained only on other lines and validated on Line_B. This gives a more realistic test of whether the model generalizes to an unseen line and prevents leakage caused by mixing rows from the same line across train and validation. If performance drops sharply on the held-out line, the ML owner should investigate line-specific process, sensor, product-mix or data-quality differences before deploying broadly."}

